@title Digital press: lease or buy
@subtitle Decision for Lucinda Marsh, owner · Meeting 2026-11-12 · Orchard Press commercial print shop

## Options
The press prints about 2.4 million pages a month. We compare two ways to get it over a four-year horizon.

cards
### Buy
- Purchase price: $412,000
- Service contract: $14,400 a year ($57,600 over four years)
- Resale value after four years: $120,000
- Net four-year cost: $349,600

### Lease
- $7,650 a month for 48 months ($367,200)
- Service included
- Deposit: two monthly payments ($15,300)
- Optional buyout at the end: $95,000

## Four-year cost
data cost = option,four-year cost; Buy,349600; Lease,367200
chart hbar cost y=four-year cost labels unit=$ title="Net four-year cost"

The lease costs $17,600 more over four years than buying.

## Risks
- Buying ties up cash we need for the new bindery. The resale value of $120,000 is a guess.
- The lease locks us in for 48 months, although the $95,000 buyout price is fixed today.

## Recommendation
We recommend the lease. It costs $17,600 more over four years, and we accept that cost to keep cash free for the new bindery.

! The lease costs $17,600 more over four years than buying.
